      "ref": "01KHVMWP",
      "slug": null,
      "title": "Write getting-started tutorial and README for external users",
      "description": "kspec has no end-to-end tutorial for new users. INSTALL.md covers setup mechanics but doesn't show the workflow. README.md is either missing or developer-focused on the kspec project itself, not on using kspec as a tool.\n\n## What's needed\n\n**README.md** — Public-facing, explains:\n- What kspec is (spec-first task management for AI-assisted development)\n- Why (shadow branch, spec-driven workflow, agent integration)\n- Quick install and init\n- Link to getting-started tutorial\n\n**Getting-started tutorial** (docs/getting-started.md or similar):\n- Walk through from 'npm install -g' to first completed task\n- Create a spec item with acceptance criteria\n- Derive a task from the spec\n- Work the task (start, implement, note, submit)\n- Create a PR with kspec trailers\n- Complete the task\n- Show the spec-first loop in action\n\n**Reference points:**\n- kynetic-bot, imgen, comfy-ecaj-nodes are real consumer projects showing actual usage patterns\n- All three independently converged on the same Quick Start: kspec init → kspec setup → kspec session start\n- The workflow skills (task-work, pr, spec) contain detailed command references that the tutorial can link to rather than duplicate\n- INSTALL.md already covers setup mechanics — tutorial should reference it, not repeat it\n\n## Scope boundaries\n- README is for the npm package / GitHub repo landing page\n- Tutorial is for humans AND agents onboarding to a new kspec project\n- Don't duplicate skill content — link to skills for detailed command syntax\n- Keep it practical with real examples, not abstract descriptions",
      "priority": 2,
      "spec_ref": null,
      "tags": [],
      "unlocks": 0
    }
